###############################################################################
# Q11 -- Computational resources
###############################################################################

# NequIP-LR needs more epochs to converge than NequIP; inference times on
# GPU and CPU are shown only in Fig. 5e, f. No numbers are given.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - NequIP-LR is a new registry method introduced here, derived from NequIP (the paper implements its framework on NequIP); its charge scheme is described as similar to 4G-HDNNP, which is not recorded as a derivation. The 4G-HDNNP comparison values in Table 1 come from Ko et al. and are not encoded.
# - The text states the Au2-MgO energy RMSEs in 'meV/A' (a typo); Table 1 gives meV/atom, which is used. The split behind Table 1 is not stated (the parity plots are on a test set), so roles are unset. Learning curves (Fig. 5c, d) are figure-only.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/maruf2025.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

